cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Kurrent Pages Benchmark"
abstract: >-
  Held-out benchmark for end-to-end transcription of German historical pages:
  Kurrent, Sütterlin, degraded Fraktur, early-modern hands, registers, and
  marginalia from 1565 to 1948. An engine gets a raw page image and returns the
  page text. The 53 scored pages are scored offline against a private,
  double-keyed transcription; only aggregates are published. The archive holds
  the preregistered protocol, the evaluation harness, the page manifest with
  source links and hashes, and the leaderboard.
